  {
    "id": "vue-components/checkbox#indeterminate-state",
    "documentId": "vue-components/checkbox",
    "heading": "Indeterminate state",
    "breadcrumb": [
      "Usage",
      "Indeterminate state",
      "Indeterminate state"
    ],
    "level": 3,
    "canonicalUrl": "https://quasar.dev/vue-components/checkbox#indeterminate-state",
    "content": "In the example below, as soon as you click on the first checkbox it starts toggling between true/false. The second checkbox, on the other hand toggles between the three states (indeterminate/true/false) with help from `toggle-indeterminate`. You can optionally set the property `indeterminate-value`, otherwise the indeterminate value will be considered `null`.\n\nExample: Indeterminate state (IndeterminateState.vue)",
    "apiReferences": [],
    "exampleReferences": [
